{
  "_comment": [
    "Shared vectors for issue #3789: which trivia is legal between a STEP type",
    "name and its '(' -- for an entity record's type name and for a typed",
    "value's. ISO 10303-21 allows a comment anywhere whitespace is allowed, and",
    "STEP whitespace is the ASCII set { ' ', \\t, \\n, \\r, 0x0B, 0x0C } -- NOT",
    "U+00A0 and friends (the TS/Rust divergence class of issue #3733).",
    "",
    "Rust half: rust/core/tests/type_paren_trivia_parity.rs (parse_entity).",
    "TS half:   packages/parser/src/type-paren-trivia.parity.test.ts",
    "           (EntityExtractor.extractEntity).",
    "",
    "trivia == 'entity': `accepted` is whether the whole record parses, and",
    "`attributeCount` its attribute count.",
    "",
    "trivia == 'typedValue': `accepted` is whether attribute 0 is read as a",
    "TYPED VALUE naming `typeName`. The two halves deliberately differ in how",
    "they REJECT: Rust's nom grammar fails the whole record, while the TS",
    "extractor's per-attribute regex falls through to its plain-string branch",
    "and hands back the raw text. Both are correct refusals to read it as a",
    "typed value, so that -- not the record-level verdict -- is what these",
    "cases pin."
  ],
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "adjacent (control)",
      "record": "#1=IFCWALL(1.);",
      "trivia": "entity",
      "accepted": true,
      "attributeCount": 1
    },
    {
      "name": "space",
      "record": "#1=IFCWALL (1.);",
      "trivia": "entity",
      "accepted": true,
      "attributeCount": 1
    },
    {
      "name": "tab",
      "record": "#1=IFCWALL\t(1.);",
      "trivia": "entity",
      "accepted": true,
      "attributeCount": 1
    },
    {
      "name": "CRLF line wrap",
      "record": "#1=IFCWALL\r\n(1.);",
      "trivia": "entity",
      "accepted": true,
      "attributeCount": 1
    },
    {
      "name": "vertical tab (0x0B)",
      "record": "#1=IFCWALL\u000b(1.);",
      "trivia": "entity",
      "accepted": true,
      "attributeCount": 1
    },
    {
      "name": "form feed (0x0C)",
      "record": "#1=IFCWALL\f(1.);",
      "trivia": "entity",
      "accepted": true,
      "attributeCount": 1
    },
    {
      "name": "block comment",
      "record": "#1=IFCWALL/* c */(1.);",
      "trivia": "entity",
      "accepted": true,
      "attributeCount": 1
    },
    {
      "name": "empty block comment",
      "record": "#1=IFCWALL/**/(1.);",
      "trivia": "entity",
      "accepted": true,
      "attributeCount": 1
    },
    {
      "name": "whitespace and comments interleaved",
      "record": "#1=IFCWALL /* a */\t/* b */\n(1.);",
      "trivia": "entity",
      "accepted": true,
      "attributeCount": 1
    },
    {
      "name": "empty argument list wrapped before ')'",
      "record": "#1=IFCWALL(\r\n);",
      "trivia": "entity",
      "accepted": true,
      "attributeCount": 0
    },
    {
      "name": "empty argument list holding only a comment",
      "record": "#1=IFCWALL(/* c */);",
      "trivia": "entity",
      "accepted": true,
      "attributeCount": 0
    },
    {
      "name": "reject: entity reference is not trivia",
      "record": "#1=IFCWALL#5(1.);",
      "trivia": "entity",
      "accepted": false
    },
    {
      "name": "reject: unterminated comment",
      "record": "#1=IFCWALL/*(1.);",
      "trivia": "entity",
      "accepted": false
    },
    {
      "name": "reject: U+00A0 is not STEP whitespace (#3733)",
      "record": "#1=IFCWALL (1.);",
      "trivia": "entity",
      "accepted": false
    },
    {
      "name": "reject: '//' is not a STEP comment",
      "record": "#1=IFCWALL//x\n(1.);",
      "trivia": "entity",
      "accepted": false
    },
    {
      "name": "reject: comments do not nest, so the trailing '*/' is junk",
      "record": "#1=IFCWALL/* /* */ */(1.);",
      "trivia": "entity",
      "accepted": false
    },
    {
      "name": "typed value adjacent (control)",
      "record": "#1=IFCWALL(IFCLABEL('a'));",
      "trivia": "typedValue",
      "accepted": true,
      "typeName": "IFCLABEL"
    },
    {
      "name": "typed value wrapped across CRLF",
      "record": "#1=IFCWALL(IFCLABEL\r\n('a'));",
      "trivia": "typedValue",
      "accepted": true,
      "typeName": "IFCLABEL"
    },
    {
      "name": "typed value separated by a vertical tab",
      "record": "#1=IFCWALL(IFCLABEL\u000b('a'));",
      "trivia": "typedValue",
      "accepted": true,
      "typeName": "IFCLABEL"
    },
    {
      "name": "typed value separated by a block comment",
      "record": "#1=IFCWALL(IFCLABEL/* c */('a'));",
      "trivia": "typedValue",
      "accepted": true,
      "typeName": "IFCLABEL"
    },
    {
      "name": "not a typed value: entity reference is not trivia",
      "record": "#1=IFCWALL(IFCLABEL#5('a'));",
      "trivia": "typedValue",
      "accepted": false
    },
    {
      "name": "not a typed value: U+00A0 is not STEP whitespace",
      "record": "#1=IFCWALL(IFCLABEL ('a'));",
      "trivia": "typedValue",
      "accepted": false
    },
    {
      "name": "not a typed value: unterminated comment",
      "record": "#1=IFCWALL(IFCLABEL/*('a'));",
      "trivia": "typedValue",
      "accepted": false
    },
    {
      "name": "not a typed value: quoted 'IFCLABEL (x)' stays a string",
      "record": "#1=IFCWALL('IFCLABEL (x)');",
      "trivia": "typedValue",
      "accepted": false,
      "stringValue": "IFCLABEL (x)"
    },
    {
      "name": "not a typed value: quoted text holding a comment stays a string",
      "record": "#1=IFCWALL('IFCLABEL/* c */(x)');",
      "trivia": "typedValue",
      "accepted": false,
      "stringValue": "IFCLABEL/* c */(x)"
    }
  ]
}
